WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.575
A few quick rules, for checking your answers and for the days you don’t have time to draw.

2
00:00:05.825 --> 00:00:09.550
A current directly with you: add its drift to your speed.

3
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:12.525
Directly against you: subtract it.

4
00:00:12.775 --> 00:00:16.500
Ten knots into a two-knot current is eight over the ground.

5
00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:22.025
A current across your track: steer up-current, by the amount the diagram gives you.

6
00:00:22.275 --> 00:00:24.350
Wind does the same thing.

7
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:30.200
When it pushes the boat sideways, that’s called leeway, and you treat it just like a current.

8
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:33.425
And how much should you trust a predicted current?

9
00:00:34.425 --> 00:00:36.525
Only until your next fix.

10
00:00:36.775 --> 00:00:39.000
Predictions are estimates.

11
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:42.400
So keep taking fixes, and keep adjusting.

12
00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:44.525
That’s lesson nine.

13
00:00:44.775 --> 00:00:47.200
Set runs from DR to fix.

14
00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:49.700
Current first, then your speed.

15
00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:51.650
Steer up-current.

16
00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:56.275
Next time, we put the whole course together in one exam problem.
